===Etymology 1===
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:knoweleche|tree=1|id=information}}
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ǵneh₃-|*leyg-|id2=jump}}
From {{inh|en|enm|knoweleche}}, {{m|enm|knowleche|t=knowledge}}, from late {{inh|en|ang|cnāwelǣċ|t=acknowledgement}}, from {{m|ang|cnāwan|t=to know}} + {{m|ang||-lǣċ(e)}}, variant of {{m|ang|-lāc|t=-ation}} modified after the related verbal suffix {{m|ang|-lǣċan}}. Related to {{cog|enm|knowelechen|t=to find out, acknowledge}}, {{cog|ang|cnāwelǣċing|t=acknowledging, acknowledgement}}.

Cognate with {{cog|fo|knáleiki|t=bravery, courage, valour}}, {{cog|is|knáleikur|t=prowess, hardihood, or physical strength}}, {{cog|fo|kunnleiki|t=knowledge, proficiency, ability, competence}}.

